// expect: 9
// SYNTAX §«Field access» through a PARAMETER whose record type is closed:
// the offset resolves from the receiver's full sorted field set, so
// `u.zeta` reads zeta even though alpha sorts first.
//
// This is the control for a measured silent wrong in its OPEN twin. Change
// `alpha: Int` below to `...` and the same call returns 7 — alpha's value —
// because an open row's offsets are computed from the KNOWN field set's own
// ordering rather than the runtime record's
// (`Hβ.lower.open-row-field-offset-from-known-set`). SYNTAX's own worked
// example of row polymorphism is that shape, so the defect sits on a
// documented surface; the red twin lands with the fix.
fn pick(u: {alpha: Int, zeta: Int}) = u.zeta

fn main() = pick({alpha: 7, zeta: 9})
